@EnriqueAllen @ChristinaPhili5 - There's a myth that only async-first cultures where we "formalize the informal" work remotely
- We think this puts too much onus on leadership to "create" culture...
- Instead, how might we create an environment your your team's natural culture expresses itself?

@johncutlefish @brettberson No worries and thanks!

Our product is meant to be used (nearly) every weekday by healthy teams. I.e. 4/5 weekdays, or 4/7 days.

We'd like to know how many users satisfy that definition, and we'd like to be able to track that over time with a chart that looks like 📈.

@pchamal Interesting question. I don’t know but I also think about
- how that ratio should be spread over time (probably not uniformly over weeks or lifetimes)
- creation is a form of self-consumption (and you upskill)

Also @alex you asked "Why is it mac only? (For the love of god?)" 😅

@remotionco is a native app! That helps us integrate more seamlessly with the OS, be less heavy on your computer, and helps us improve audio/video quality.

I love PCs (am gamer) and we're working on it.

@AntoniZolciak @remotionco Hey Antoni, cofounder @remotionco here.

How are you thinking about using it, and what new habits does that entail?

Let us know how we can help!

@sidsverma @tjack @Tandem_HQ @remotionco Secondarily:
- We’re more privacy-oriented. E.g. we don’t automatically share what app or doc you’re in.
- They’re in Electron which makes efficient, high quality video chat harder to attain.

@sidsverma @tjack @Tandem_HQ @remotionco Fun example: What do you do if you want some company while WFH?

Tandem: Join the watercooler channel (probably empty though outside of scheduled times).

Remotion: Set yourself to "Open to chat", or click someone who's Open.

@ramikalai @tjack @around_hq @remotionco Quick way to see the difference:

Around's UI only shows when you're in a video call.

Remotion puts a Shortlist of your closest collaborators on your desktop. https://t.co/2L1LcUxiZE

@ramikalai @tjack @around_hq Cofounder @remotionco here 👋

Around is focused on in-meeting-AI features.

Remotion is focused on helping you get into *more* quick video chats. To do that you need team awareness -&gt; selfies on your desktop

@jornvandijk Very async teams collaborate on ideas in pull requests that get reviewed and merged. (E.g. Gitlab supposedly)

Moderately async teams keep all meaningful conversation in Asana &amp; co.

More sync teams chat in Zoom and maybe add presence like Sococo/Remotion. (I work at Remotion)

@suzenfylke @freialobo @remotionco 👋 that was a fun plane flight!

@remotionco (https://t.co/LpExr6eObK) helps distributed work not feel remote with presence and quick video chats.
Including both syncs and “syncs”.
Would love to show you a demo!

@jlogic @LiamBoogar Focusing on comms (loneliness for remote seems uncontroversial):

Great teams (remote or not) develop structured, async processes to execute better.

However, unstructured live touchpoints support team building and innovation. These are much harder for remote teams. https://t.co/EKFDKIyqRW

@Connor @bthdonohue Distributed work shouldn’t feel remote.

Creating a feeling of presence and chatting face to face outside of scheduled transactional meetings is key.

(I’m working on a product to help teams get this right. Would love your feedback: https://t.co/LpExr6eObK)
